STEP 3 — Display Patient Records

File:

hospital/patients.html

JavaScript:

hospital/js/patient-list.js

Responsibility:

Display existing patient records.

The patient list does NOT create patient records.

Patient creation belongs to Member 2.

Data source:

patient-data.js

Function used:

getPatients()

The patient list gets the patient array and displays
the records in an HTML table.


Basic flow:

patients.html
    ↓
patient-list.js
    ↓
getPatients()
    ↓
patients array
    ↓
HTML table


DOM CONCEPT:

The DOM represents the HTML page as objects that JavaScript
can interact with.

Example:

document.getElementById("patientTableBody")

finds the <tbody> element.

document.createElement("tr")

creates a new table row.

appendChild()

adds the new row to the table.


The first implementation intentionally uses basic DOM
operations rather than a complicated UI system.


Deleted patients:

The list checks:

patient.deleted

If it is true, the patient is skipped.

Therefore the normal patient list shows active records only.

This prepares the application for the soft-delete behavior
planned for US004.


