ALL PATIENTS — CREATED AND UPDATED

The All Patients table displays:

- Patient ID
- Name
- DOB
- Gender
- Mobile
- Created
- Updated
- Action

createdAt:
Shows when the patient was originally created.

updatedAt:
Shows when the patient was last edited.

If updatedAt does not exist, the table displays "-".

patient-list.js contains a small formatDateTime()
function to convert the stored ISO date into a readable
date and time.

Example:

Created: 14/09/2026, 10:30 AM
Updated: 14/09/2026, 10:45 AM

US005 — VIEW ACTIVE PATIENTS

The All Patients page displays active patients.

Deleted patients are not displayed.

The page shows:
- Active patient count
- Patient table
- 5 patients per page
- Previous button
- Next button
- Current page information

PATIENTS_PER_PAGE = 5

Pagination works by using:
- currentPage
- slice()
- Math.ceil()

filter() is used to create a list containing
only active patients.

Example:

deleted = false
→ patient is shown

deleted = true
→ patient is hidden


Patient list flow:

getPatients()
→ filter active patients
→ count active patients
→ select current page
→ display table


US006 — SEARCH PATIENT BY ID

Search is part of the All Patients page.

The user can search using Patient ID.

Search:
- ignores uppercase/lowercase
- removes spaces at the beginning/end
- works with the Search button
- works with Enter
- has a Clear button
- searches active patients only

Deleted patients are not searchable.

Search and pagination work together.

When a search is performed:
currentPage is reset to 1.

If no matching active patient exists:

"No active patient found."

Clear search:
- removes the search text
- resets currentPage to 1
- displays all active patients again.

patient-list.js is responsible for displaying
and searching the active patient list.




